WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.960
Narrator: The kids from
"Stranger Things" may be going

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.390
through some changes.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.750
Eleven and the gang are now teenagers,

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.260
but Hawkins seems to be stuck in the midst

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.260
of a never-ending monster infestation.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.380
Netflix released the
first full-length trailer

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.110
for the third season of "Stranger Things."

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.070
Here's everything you might've missed.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.192
The third season will take place in 1985,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.400
six months after the events in season 2.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.570
We know this because Dustin is back

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.097
from some kind of science camp...

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:34.970
Dustin: At least someone's happy I'm home.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.835
Narrator: called Camp Know Where,

00:00:37.835 --> 00:00:39.870
and he's wearing a hat that says '85

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.120
on the computer screen.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.640
The song that plays in the beginning

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.707
is also from 1985,

00:00:44.707 --> 00:00:47.447
Mötley Crüe's "Home Sweet Home."

00:00:48.509 --> 00:00:50.640
♪ Long and winding road ♪

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.890
In addition to the original cast,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.020
we have some fresh faces
that we get a glimpse

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.730
of for the first time.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.320
Cary Elwes from "The Princess
Bride" plays Hawkins' mayor,

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.010
whom the residents don't seem

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.360
to be happy with

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.180
and whose campaign sign
is strikingly similar

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.750
to Donald Trump's.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.950
Maya Hawke, daughter of Uma Thurman

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.070
and Ethan Hawke,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.870
plays a character named Robin.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.310
Maya will also appear
in Quentin Tarantino's

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.190
"Once Upon a Time in Hollywood."

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.500
And Jake Busey, Gary Busey's son,

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.293
will play someone named Bruce.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.582
Dustin comes home to see
his Tommy Atomic robot

00:01:26.582 --> 00:01:29.170
emerge from the shadows.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.330
It's followed by R2-D2,
two tanks, a train,

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.690
and Ultra Magnus, who's a Transformer.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.390
The toys move completely on their own,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.700
but it turns out to
just be a surprise party

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.483
with Eleven using her powers.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.410
Dustin attacks Lucas using
the Farrah Fawcett hairspray

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.193
that Steve gave him in season 2.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.000
Lucas has a little sister named Erica

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.920
who's shown in multiple shots,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.560
so she may play a bigger role

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.463
in season 3.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.000
The kids are all clearly going

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.600
through some growing pains.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.100
A remix of The Who's "Baba O'Riley"

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.330
is playing through much of the trailer,

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.830
likely to support the characters

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.192
becoming part of this "teenage wasteland."

00:02:12.192 --> 00:02:16.025
♪ It's only teenage wasteland ♪

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:18.910
Everyone seems to have a new summer job.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.790
Nancy and Jonathan appear to be applying

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.460
to or working for the local newspaper,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.140
or they're just trying to alert the press

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.890
of something going on in Hawkins.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.550
Billy is a lifeguard at the Hawkins pool.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.580
One of the episodes is titled "The Case

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.980
of the Missing Lifeguard."

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.020
This could be a reference

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.420
to the lifeguard that
passes Billy at the pool

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.450
who's later seen in peril.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.850
Steve is working alongside Robin

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.440
at an ice cream shop called Scoops Ahoy.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.570
Much of the season looks like

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:47.260
it will take place at
the local Starcourt Mall,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.790
which we saw in an earlier
teaser for the show,

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.080
and the finale is actually
called "The Battle of

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.630
Starcourt," so something big is expected

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.040
to happen here.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.000
Part of the season will probably
revolve around a carnival

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.370
called the Fun Fair.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.300
We get a shot of a man with a gun

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.340
walking through a hall of mirrors,

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.330
showing that things will turn sinister.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.163
At one point,

00:03:07.163 --> 00:03:10.400
you can see Hopper standing
in front of a Gravitron,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.470
a classic 1980s carnival ride.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.640
Eleven is back in the Upside Down.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.300
She's also wearing a blue
hair tie on her wrist.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.340
This used to belong to
Sheriff Hopper's daughter

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.540
before she died,

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.560
which we learned in season 2.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.830
So he must have passed it
on to her at some point.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.470
There's also a very brief glimpse

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.280
of Eleven standing blindfolded

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.870
in front of a grocery store freezer

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.220
full of Eggo waffles.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.053
In every season,

00:03:34.053 --> 00:03:35.550
there's at least one shot of Eleven

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.110
going straight for the waffles.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.620
In one shot,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.770
Eleven is wearing a yellow shirt

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.130
by the blue sea.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.917
A previous teaser included
the mysterious phrase

00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:50.060
"When blue and yellow meet in the west."

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.820
This could be the moment referenced,

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.570
but it could be when the
blue and yellow hands

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.690
on the clock meet at the Starcourt Mall

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.690
as shown in another teaser.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.190
We also get a first glimpse

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.930
of this season's monster.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.210
So far each season of the show has tried

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.880
to top itself in terms of its monsters.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.187
In one brief shot,

00:04:08.187 --> 00:04:10.150
we see the creature transform right

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.080
in front of Jonathan.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.550
It starts off as a slimy ball.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:14.590
A few shots later,

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.580
we see the creature in full.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:18.290
It's much different from the Demogorgon

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.960
from season 1 and the
Demodogs from season 2.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.570
This one has a very spiderlike appearance.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.530
All the other monsters
from the show have drawn

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.763
inspiration from Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:04:29.673 --> 00:04:31.339
Mike: The Demogorgon!

00:04:31.339 --> 00:04:32.240
Narrator: It's unclear which monster

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.620
this is inspired by,

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.440
but there are several possibilities.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.273
In one shot,

00:04:36.273 --> 00:04:37.700
we see a bunch of rats scurrying

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.988
into a warehouse.

00:04:38.988 --> 00:04:41.330
Rats are typically associated

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.140
with disease and the plague.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.510
Is there some sort of infection spreading

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.420
around town?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.010
It looks like Billy may have caught

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.860
whatever it is here.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.290
We won't know anything for sure

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.630
until season 3 comes out

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.513
on July Fourth.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.460
Did you notice anything we didn't?

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.963
Let us know in the comments.

